s.\",\n    \"priorFindingStatuses\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"SV-001\",\n        \"status\": \"needs-human-ruling\",\n        \"rationale\": \"The module-scope thread id was removed, but reload for no-flag and --resume now reattaches to the cwd's most-recent registry row rather than reconstructing from the resolved thread id required by AC-1.5. The implementor artifact and code both identify this as an Epic-1 convenience with a known concurrent same-cwd limitation and defer precise lineage to Feature 2+.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"SV-002\",\n        \"status\": \"needs-human-ruling\",\n        \"rationale\": \"The production path now shows the cwd-scoped title/created/id list through ctx.ui.notify, but it still auto-selects the most recent thread. AC-1.7 requires resolving the operator's selection; the implementor records this as a spec deviation because PI v0.79.2 exposes no interactive selection surface.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"newFindings\": [],\n    \"openFindings\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"SV-001\",\n        \"severity\": \"major\",\n        \"title\": \"Reload reconstruction still does not use the resolved thread id for no-flag and --resume reloads\",\n        \"evidence\": \"AC-1.5 requires reload reconstruction from durable state, specifically the resolved thread id (story lines 51-53). The revised resolveReloadThread handles --session by id, but for no-flag and --resume it lists threads by cwd and chooses listed.value.at(-1) at packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts:118-147. The implementor artifact records that a concurrent same-cwd session could be selected instead and defers precise reload lineage to Feature 2+. The test at packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts:335-370 proves only the single-thread-in-cwd case, not reconstruction from the prior resolved thread id.\",\n        \"affectedFiles\": [\n          \"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts\",\n          \"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\n          \"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\"\n        ],\n        \"requirementIds\": [\n          \"AC-1.5\",\n          \"TC-1.5\"\n        ],\n        \"recommendedFixScope\": \"human-ruling\",\n        \"blocking\": true\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"SV-002\",\n        \"severity\": \"major\",\n        \"title\": \"Production --resume still does not resolve an operator selection\",\n        \"evidence\": \"AC-1.7 requires --resume/-r to list cwd-scoped threads with title and creation time and resolve the operator's selection (story lines 59-61; tech design lines 231 and 251-253). The revised defaultSelectThread shows the list via ctx.ui.notify but then returns mostRecent.threadId at packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:157-176. The production test asserts notification plus most-recent behavior at packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts:255-290. The implementor artifact records this as a spec deviation because the available PI UI surface has notify but no interactive input.\",\n        \"affectedFiles\": [\n          \"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\n          \"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/picker.ts\",\n          \"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\"\n        ],\n        \"requirementIds\": [\n          \"AC-1.7\",\n          \"TC-1.7\"\n        ],\n        \"recommendedFixScope\": \"human-ruling\",\n        \"blocking\": true\n      }\n    ],\n    \"requirementCoverage\": {\n      \"verified\": [\n        \"AC-1.1 / TC-1.1: no-flag session_start creates one cwd/title registry thread and one background LHC instance; lifecycle tests and pi-lhc verify pass.\",\n        \"AC-1.2 / TC-1.2: existing --session launch attaches to the existing thread and creates no second thread.\",\n        \"AC-1.3 / TC-1.3 plain-data holder: connector snapshot remains structuredClone-able across fresh ctx objects.\",\n        \"AC-1.4 / TC-1.4: shutdown dispose flush preserves pre-shutdown intake events across re-resolve.\",\n        \"AC-1.6 / TC-1.6: launch modes and bad/ambiguous id behavior remain covered.\",\n        \"A-8 registry support remains covered by lhc threads-a8 focused test.\"\n      ],\n      \"unverified\": [\n        \"AC-1.5 / TC-1.5 for no-flag and --resume reload reconstruction from the resolved thread id; current implementation uses cwd-most-recent registry selection.\",\n        \"AC-1.7 / TC-1.7 production operator selection; current implementation presents choices but auto-selects most recent.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"gatesRun\": [\n      {\n        \"command\": \"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify\",\n        \"result\": \"pass\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"command\": \"pnpm --filter pi-lhc verify-all\",\n        \"result\": \"pass\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"command\": \"pnpm --filter pi-lhc exec vitest run test/lifecycle/instance.test.ts test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\",\n        \"result\": \"pass\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"command\": \"pnpm --filter lhc exec vitest run test/threads-a8.test.ts\",\n        \"result\": \"pass\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"productionPathFindings\": [\n      \"Reload production path for no-flag/--resume uses cwd-most-recent registry selection, not the prior resolved thread id.\",\n      \"Production --resume presents choices through notify but auto-selects most recent; there is no real operator selection in the production path.\"\n    ],\n    \"recommendedNextStep\": \"needs-human-ruling\",\n    \"recommendedFixScope\": \"human-ruling\",\n    \"openQuestions\": [\n      \"Does Lee accept cwd-most-recent registry reattach as satisfying AC-1.5 for Story 1 despite the known concurrent same-cwd limitation?\",\n      \"Does Lee accept notify-list plus most-recent default as satisfying AC-1.7 until PI exposes an interactive selection surface?\"\n    ],\n    \"additionalObservations\": [\n      \"The story and epic gates pass: pi-lhc verify and verify-all both passed with 33 tests.\",\n      \"The prior module-scope reload memory implementation is gone; the remaining SV-001 issue is the replacement behavior, not retained module state.\",\n      \"The fail-closed observeOnlyProvider remains unchanged from the prior review and was not part of the follow-up fix surface.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"errors\": [],\n  \"warnings\": [],\n  \"artifacts\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"result-envelope\",\n      \"path\": \"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/014-verify.json\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"startedAt\": \"2026-06-14T06:11:39.905Z\",\n  \"finishedAt\": \"2026-06-14T06:13:34.016Z\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
