{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260614213908bc19479f181a450b","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the implementation. Let me write my epic review. I need to assess:\n\n1. Cross-story consistency - looking for drift between stories\n2. Architecture alignment - checking against tech design contracts\n3. Production path audit - fake adapters, shims, placeholders\n4. Epic coverage assessment - what's been covered\n5. Blocking findings - issues that need to be fixed\n6. Non-blocking findings - observations\n7. Unresolved items\n8. Gate result\n\nFrom my analysis:\n\n**Cross-Story Consistency:**\n- The implementation is consistent across stories. The module boundaries are well-defined (lifecycle, capture, inference, verify).\n- The plain-data-only rule (AC-1.3) is consistently enforced - only SessionState is held, no PI context objects.\n- The idempotency key construction is consistent throughout capture and replay.\n- Turn derivation logic is consistent - turn_end only at agent_end, ignoring PI's per-step turn_end.\n\n**Architecture Alignment:**\n- The implementation follows the tech design's module architecture.\n- The hook rail in index.ts correctly routes to the appropriate modules.\n- The converter is properly split into map-message, turn-accumulator, and idempotency.\n- The inference routing uses the real PI model registry (in tests via fakes, in production via dynamic import).\n- The capture failure isolation matches the design (gap on writable thread, health signal on store unavailable).\n\n**Production Path Audit:**\n- Real paths:\n  - LHC SDK is real (no mocking)\n  - SQLite persistence is real (temp threads in tests)\n  - The converter path is real\n  - The inference host routing will use real PI model registry via dynamic import (@earendil-works/pi-ai)\n  \n- Test-only fakes (acceptable):\n  - Deterministic ModelCall fakes in test/fixtures/model-call.ts\n  - Synthetic corpus builders in test/fixtures/synthetic.ts\n  - Observe-only provider in replay.ts (appropriate for verification)\n  \n- Potential concerns:\n  - The PI types are local (pi/types.ts) due to uninstalled @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent - documented deviation\n  - The pi-ai types are local (inference/pi-ai.ts) for the same reason - documented deviation\n  - These are acceptable temporary measures given the package isn't installed\n\n**Epic Coverage:**\n- Story 0 (Foundation): Extension loads, registers hooks, plain-data state holder\n- Story 1 (Lifecycle): Instance init/dispose, thread resolution, reload, picker\n- Story 2 (Capture): Converter with turn derivation, idempotency, runtime changes, parallel correlation\n- Story 3 (Verification): Replay harness, read-back compare, deterministic\n\n, inspect surfaces\n- Story 4 (Fork): Fork detection, replay seeding, source immutability, derived form handling\n- Story 5 (Inference): Model call function routing through PI registry, failure classification, multi-lane support\n- Story 6 (Validation): Startup validation with registry probing, assignment configuration\n\n**Gate Status**\n- Tests: 142 passed across 20 files\n- Build/typecheck/lint/boundaries: all clear\n- Epic gate passes\n\n**Observations**\n- Validation messages about unreachable derivation lanes are expected during testing—there's no real PI model registry available\n- Local PI and pi-ai types are temporary placeholders until the packages are installed\n- Story 2's known edge case around id-less idempotency keys (same content, same position) is documented and accepted as unreachable on the real hook path\n\n**Summary**\nThe epic is ready to pass. All critical functionality is implemented with proper separation of concerns, real persistence paths where needed, and appropriate test fakes at boundaries. The temporary type workarounds are well-documented and will be resolved when the actual PI packages become available.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0d8ccb7-eaf7-457e-b1b4-b7920fccc144","uuid":"5e69ef19-f6f7-4e00-b5b3-d1f8882c27df"}
