{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260614213908bc19479f181a450b","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-4.7","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive review of the epic implementation, I'll now provide my epic review verdict.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"pass\",\n  \"crossStoryFindings\": [\n    \"Cross-story consistency is strong across the implementation. The plain-data-only rule (AC-1.3) is consistently enforced - only SessionState is retained across hooks, no PI context objects.\",\n    \"Turn derivation logic is consistent throughout - turn_end events are emitted only at agent_end, ignoring PI's per-step turn_end boundaries.\",\n    \"Idempotency key construction uses the same tiered approach (entryId → toolCallId → responseId → fallback) across capture, replay, and fork paths.\",\n    \"Module boundaries are clean and well-respected: lifecycle, capture, inference, and verify surfaces maintain their separation of concerns.\"\n  ],\n  \"architectureFindings\": [\n    \"Implementation closely follows the tech design's module architecture. The hook rail in index.ts correctly routes to appropriate handlers.\",\n    \"The converter is properly decomposed into map-message (pure), turn-accumulator (state machine), idempotency (pure), and converter (orchestration) as designed.\",\n    \"Capture failure isolation matches the design contract: writable thread failures produce durable gaps via runtime_note events; store-unavailable failures surface as health signals.\",\n    \"The inference routing correctly treats provider/model as opaque routing keys, with real PI model registry resolution via dynamic import.\",\n    \"Fork implementation follows the Epic 1 design: detection via session_before_fork hook with PI session tree fallback, seeding by event replay, source thread immutability verified.\"\n  ],\n  \"epicCoverageAssessment\": [\n    \"Story 0 (Foundation): Complete - extension loads, registers Epic 1 observe-only hook rail, plain-data state holder established, fixture infrastructure in place.\",\n    \"Story 1 (Lifecycle): Complete - instance init/dispose with flush, thread resolution by launch mode (new/--session/--continue), reload reconstruction from durable registry, cwd-scoped picker.\",\n    \"Story 2 (Capture): Complete - PI→LHC event mapping with content-part fan-out, turn derivation (one LHC turn per agent run), parallel tool correlation by toolCallId, error-result capture, graceful abort handling, runtime-change capture (model_select/thinking_level_select), idempotency-keyed dedup, capture-failure isolation.\",\n    \"Story 3 (Verification): Complete - corpus replay through real converter, read-back comparison against fixtures (events/messages/turns/order), deterministic replay verified, inspect overview/health surfaces.\",\n    \"Story 4 (Fork): Complete - fork detection (hook + PI session tree fallback), new thread seeded by replay to fork point, source thread immutability verified, derived forms requeue (v1 correctness, reuse optimization deferred).\",\n    \"Story 5 (Inference): Complete - ModelCall function over PI model registry, multi-lane routing, provider-error classification (auth/invalid_request terminal, rate_limit/timeout/network retryable, thrown→other), empty_output handling by LHC adapter.\",\n    \"Story 6 (Validation): Complete - all seven assignments validated against PI registry before first derivation use, unreachable lane reporting with kind+(provider,model)+fix, headless-safe reporting (ctx.ui.notify when available, stderr fallback), capture continues on validation failure.\"\n  ],\n  \"productionPathFindings\": [\n    \"Real LHC SDK execution path confirmed - no LHC mocking, all persistence runs against real SQLite temp threads in tests.\",\n    \"Real converter path exercised - mapMessage, TurnAccumulator, and capture functions are production code, not test doubles.\",\n    \"Real fork seeding path - seedFork uses actual intakeStream.messageEvents for replay, not a mock write path.\",\n    \"Real inspect/health surfaces - overview and health reads come from LHC SDK, not faked responses.\",\n    \"PI types deviation is documented and temporary - local declarations in src/pi/types.ts mirror verified v0.79.2 shapes; will swap to real @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent imports when package is installed (Epic 2/4).\",\n    \"pi-ai types deviation is documented and temporary - local declarations in src/inference/pi-ai.ts; production uses dynamic import of @earendil-works/pi-ai with graceful failure when unavailable.\",\n    \"Deterministic ModelCall fakes in test/fixtures/model-call.ts are appropriate test-boundary instrumentation, not production-path shims.\",\n    \"Observe-only provider in verify/replay.ts is appropriate for verification - it correctly fails derivations rather than fabricating text, matching Epic 1's observe-only contract.\",\n    \"Startup validation warnings about 'unknown_model' during test runs are expected - tests run without a real PI model registry; the validation logic itself correctly probes registry.find/hasConfiguredAuth.\"\n  ],\n  \"blockingFindings\": [],\n  \"nonBlockingFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NF-001\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"Documented idempotency edge case for identity-less events\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Story 2 implementation log notes SV-001 residual: a truly identity-less event (no entryId AND no source position AND same content) cannot satisfy both stable-on-redelivery AND unique-per-occurrence constraints. Real PI message_end always carries a stable entry id per research line 142, so this edge is unreachable on the production hook path.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-2.6\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"human-ruling\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NF-002\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"PI extension input/selection API unavailable for --resume picker\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Story 1 implementation log notes SV-002: PI v0.79.2 exposes no interactive input/selection surface. Production --resume presents candidates via ctx.ui.notify and auto-selects most-recent. Exact operator selection and exact-prior-thread reload are deferred until PI provides the API.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/picker.ts\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-1.7\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"fresh-fix-path\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NF-003\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"Derived form reuse optimization deferred for v1\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Story 4 fork implementation always requeues derived forms rather than copying/reusing ready forms. Fork correctness is preserved (AC-3.3 permits reuse 'may'), but provenance-identity safety is not yet implemented. Reuse optimization deferred to Epic 2+.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-3.3\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"fresh-fix-path\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unresolvedItems\": [\n    \"M0 corpora for Story 3 fixtures - current implementation uses synthetic builders; test coverage widens when M0 delivers recorded PI sessions.\",\n    \"Image/file-reference handling decision (A-7) - interim implementation degrades unsupported parts to runtime_note events with omission text; safe default that can extend intake schema when M0 decides.\",\n    \"PI extension input/selection API - upstream request filed for real --resume picker and exact-thread reload capability.\",\n    \"createSdk→initLhc rename (A-4) - mechanical rename pending in lhc package; pi-lhc uses initLhc wrapper as documented in tech design.\"\n  ],\n  \"gateResult\": \"pass\"\n}\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a0d8ccb7-eaf7-457e-b1b4-b7920fccc144","uuid":"6bcee944-a5cf-44a3-bc29-aeb88ee2f941"}
