everity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"PI extension input/selection API unavailable for --resume picker\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Story 1 implementation log notes SV-002: PI v0.79.2 exposes no interactive input/selection surface. Production --resume presents candidates via ctx.ui.notify and auto-selects most-recent. Exact operator selection and exact-prior-thread reload are deferred until PI provides the API.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/picker.ts\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-1.7\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"fresh-fix-path\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NF-003\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"Derived form reuse optimization deferred for v1\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Story 4 fork implementation always requeues derived forms rather than copying/reusing ready forms. Fork correctness is preserved (AC-3.3 permits reuse 'may'), but provenance-identity safety is not yet implemented. Reuse optimization deferred to Epic 2+.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts\"],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\"AC-3.3\"],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"fresh-fix-path\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unresolvedItems\": [\n    \"M0 corpora for Story 3 fixtures - current implementation uses synthetic builders; test coverage widens when M0 delivers recorded PI sessions.\",\n    \"Image/file-reference handling decision (A-7) - interim implementation degrades unsupported parts to runtime_note events with omission text; safe default that can extend intake schema when M0 decides.\",\n    \"PI extension input/selection API - upstream request filed for real --resume picker and exact-thread reload capability.\",\n    \"createSdk→initLhc rename (A-4) - mechanical rename pending in lhc package; pi-lhc uses initLhc wrapper as documented in tech design.\"\n  ],\n  \"gateResult\": \"pass\"\n}\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"a0d8ccb7-eaf7-457e-b1b4-b7920fccc144","total_cost_usd":0.8476779999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":104025,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":464256,"output_tokens":3817,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":104025,"outputTokens":3817,"cacheReadInputTokens":464256,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.8476779999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"035b5e4d-c8a7-4eb6-b23b-a6a9f78ce072"}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_53","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"The implemented epic is mostly coherent across Stories 2-6, and the configured Story/Epic gates pass. The remaining cross-story issue is Story 1 thread identity: reload and resume are foundational to every later capture, fork, verification, and derivation flow, so accepting cwd-most-recent behavior changes the meaning of a recorded thread across the whole epic.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"AC-1.5 says reload reconstructs from durable state, specifically the resolved thread id. The implementation reattaches no-flag and --resume reloads by cwd-most-recent registry row instead of the prior resolved thread id.\",\"AC-1.7 says --resume resolves the operator's selection. The production path presents candidates through ctx.ui.notify, then auto-selects the most recent thread. The tested production behavior matches that deviation, not the literal acceptance criterion.\",\"No context hook is registered for Epic 1, capture/inference/fork/validation modules are wired through real LHC surfaces, and tests exercise temp SQLite threads rather than mocked src modules.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Flow 1 is partially covered but blocked on AC-1.5 and AC-1.7 production behavior.\",\"Flows 2, 3, 4, 5, and 6 have direct source/tests and latest story-verifier evidence showing pass, including capture gaps, fork replay, model-call routing, startup validation, and replay/inspect verification.\",\"The M0 corpus breadth remains a named spec input; current replay fixtures are synthetic/fixture-backed but the Story 3 implementation drives the real converter and intake path.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"Material production-path finding: reload for no-flag and --resume uses cwd-most-recent registry selection, which can attach capture to the wrong thread when more than one thread exists for the cwd.\",\"Material production-path finding: production --resume has no real operator selection path; it notifies the list and auto-selects most recent.\",\"No material fake model adapter or fabricated completion path remains in production inference: createModelCall resolves through PI modelRegistry and dynamically imports @earendil-works/pi-ai, returning classified failures if unavailable. Test fakes are confined to test fixtures.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Reload can reattach to the wrong cwd thread\",\"evidence\":\"Epic AC-1.5 requires reload reconstruction from the resolved thread id (docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:137). resolveReloadThread documents no-flag/--resume reload as cwd-most-recent and returns listed.value.at(-1) (packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts:118, packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts:141). The production test proves only the single-thread cwd case (packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts:335). Latest Story 1 verifier also marked this needs-human-ruling in artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/014-verify.json.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/014-verify.json\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.5\",\"TC-1.5\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"EV-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Production --resume does not resolve an operator selection\",\"evidence\":\"Epic AC-1.7 requires --resume to resolve the operator's selection (docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/epic.md:141). defaultSelectThread states PI lacks an interactive selection surface, notifies candidates, then returns mostRecent.threadId (packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:181, packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:195). The production test asserts the most-recent default as the selected thread (packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts:255, packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts:289). Latest Story 1 verifier marked this needs-human-ruling in artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/014-verify.json.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/picker.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\",\"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/014-verify.json\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.7\",\"TC-1.7\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Human ruling needed: accept or reject cwd-most-recent reload reattach for no-flag/--resume launches.\",\"Human ruling needed: accept or reject notify-list plus most-recent default as the v1 production --resume behavior until PI exposes an interactive selection API.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}"}}
