{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":89176,"duration_api_ms":87727,"ttft_ms":3100,"ttft_stream_ms":3092,"time_to_request_ms":44,"num_turns":8,"result":"Based on my analysis of the epic artifacts, independent reviewer results, and the Story 1 verification evidence, I can now produce the canonical epic review.\n\nThe key disagreement is between:\n- **epic-reviewer-1**: Passed the epic, viewing these as documented acceptable deviations\n- **epic-reviewer-2**: Blocked on EV-001 and EV-002, both documented but marked as requiring human ruling\n\nAfter reviewing the evidence:\n1. **EV-001 is supported**: AC-1.5 explicitly requires reconstruction from \"the resolved thread id,\" but the implementation uses \"cwd-most-recent\" for no-flag/--resume reloads. The code comments (line 118-121 of thread-resolution.ts) acknowledge this as a convenience with a \"known concurrent same-cwd limitation.\"\n\n2. **EV-002 is supported**: AC-1.7 requires resolving \"the operator's selection,\" but the implementation auto-selects most-recent (index.ts lines 181-200). The code comments (lines 181-190) acknowledge this as \"a precise spec deviation\" because PI lacks an interactive input surface.\n\nThese are documented deviations that both reviewers identified. The question is whether they should block. The default position stated in the reverifier prompt is: \"If one or more reviewers returned block, default conservative: do not downgrade a blocker unless the code and epic evidence explicitly disprove it.\"\n\nThe evidence shows the deviations are real and acknowledged in the code itself. Since both are marked \"human-ruling\" scope by the original verifier, and no human ruling accepting these deviations is present in the artifacts, I must preserve the block.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"block\",\n  \"reviewerLabels\": [\"epic-reviewer-1\", \"epic-reviewer-2\"],\n  \"reconciliationSummary\": \"Reviewer-1 assessed the epic as complete with three non-blocking observations about documented limitations. Reviewer-2 identified two major blocking findings (EV-001, EV-002) concerning Story 1 thread identity on reload and --resume operator selection. Both findings are supported by code evidence: the implementation explicitly acknowledges cwd-most-recent reload reattach as an Epic-1 convenience with concurrent same-cwd limitations (thread-resolution.ts:118-121) and most-recent auto-selection as a spec deviation due to PI's lack of interactive input (index.ts:181-190). The Story 1 verification artifact (014-verify.json) confirms both SV-001 and SV-002 are 'needs-human-ruling' with gates passing but production behavior deviating from literal AC requirements. Because Reviewer-2 returned block and the deviations are acknowledged in-code with no human-ruling accepting them, the conservative position preserves the block.\",\n  \"crossStoryFindings\": [\n    \"Cross-story consistency is strong across Stories 2-6. The plain-data-only rule (AC-1.3) is consistently enforced — only SessionState is retained across hooks, no PI context objects.\",\n    \"Turn derivation logic is consistent throughout — turn_end events are emitted only at agent_end, ignoring PI's per-step turn_end boundaries (AC-2.2).\",\n    \"Idempotency key construction uses the same tiered approach (entryId → toolCallId → responseId → fallback) across capture, replay, and fork paths (AC-2.6).\",\n    \"Module boundaries are clean: lifecycle, capture, inference, and verify surfaces maintain separation of concerns with no internal module mocking.\"\n  ],\n  \"architectureFindings\": [\n    \"Implementation closely follows the tech design's module architecture. The hook rail in index.ts correctly routes to appropriate handlers.\",\n    \"The converter is properly decomposed into map-message (pure), turn-accumulator (state machine), idempotency (pure), and converter (orchestration) as designed.\",\n    \"Capture failure isolation matches the design contract: writable thread failures produce durable gaps via runtime_note events; store-unavailable failures surface as health signals (AC-2.7).\",\n    \"Inference routing correctly treats provider/model as opaque routing keys, with real PI model registry resolution via dynamic import.\",\n    \"Fork implementation follows the Epic 1 design: detection via session_before_fork hook with PI session tree fallback, seeding by event replay, source thread immutability verified (AC-3.1, AC-3.2).\",\n    \"The two blocking deviations are acknowledged design positions taken in Epic 1 as conveniences pending Feature 2+ permanent lineage metadata.\"\n  ],\n  \"epicCoverageAssessment\": [\n    \"Story 0 (Foundation): Complete — extension loads, registers Epic 1 observe-only hook rail, plain-data state holder established, fixture infrastructure in place.\",\n    \"Story 1 (Lifecycle): Complete with acknowledged deviations — instance init/dispose with flush, thread resolution by launch mode (new/--session/--continue), reload reconstruction uses cwd-most-recent for no-flag/--resume (SV-001 documented deviation), cwd-scoped picker with most-recent auto-selection (SV-002 documented deviation).\",\n    \"Story 2 (Capture): Complete — PI→LHC event mapping with content-part fan-out, turn derivation (one LHC turn per agent run), parallel tool correlation by toolCallId, error-result capture, graceful abort handling, runtime-change capture, idempotency-keyed dedup, capture-failure isolation (AC-2.1 through AC-2.8).\",\n    \"Story 3 (Verification): Complete — corpus replay through real converter, read-back comparison against fixtures, deterministic replay verified, inspect overview/health surfaces (AC-6.1 through AC-6.3).\",\n    \"Story 4 (Fork): Complete — fork detection (hook + PI session tree fallback), new thread seeded by replay to fork point, source thread immutability verified, derived forms requeue (AC-3.1 through AC-3.3).\",\n    \"Story 5 (Inference): Complete — ModelCall function over PI model registry, multi-lane routing, provider-error classification (auth/invalid_request terminal, rate_limit/timeout/network retryable, thrown→other), empty_output handling by LHC adapter (AC-4.1 through AC-4.5).\",\n    \"Story 6 (Validation): Complete — all seven assignments validated against PI registry before first derivation use, unreachable lane reporting with kind+(provider,model)+fix, headless-safe reporting (ctx.ui.notify when available, stderr fallback), capture continues on validation failure (AC-5.1 through AC-5.6).\"\n  ],\n  \"productionPathFindings\": [\n    \"Real LHC SDK execution path confirmed — no LHC mocking, all persistence runs against real SQLite temp threads in tests.\",\n    \"Real converter path exercised — mapMessage, TurnAccumulator, and capture functions are production code, not test doubles.\",\n    \"Real fork seeding path — seedFork uses actual intakeStream.messageEvents for replay, not a mock write path.\",\n    \"Real inspect/health surfaces — overview and health reads come from LHC SDK, not faked responses.\",\n    \"PI types deviation is documented and temporary — local declarations in src/pi/types.ts mirror verified v0.79.2 shapes; will swap to real @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent imports when package is installed (Epic 2/4).\",\n    \"pi-ai types deviation is documented and temporary — local declarations in src/inference/pi-ai.ts; production uses dynamic import of @earendil-works/pi-ai with graceful failure when unavailable.\",\n    \"DETERMINED PRODUCTION PATH DEVIATION: Reload for no-flag and --resume uses cwd-most-recent registry selection rather than reconstructing from a prior resolved thread id (EV-001). The implementation acknowledges this as an Epic-1 convenience with concurrent same-cwd limitations.\",\n    \"DETERMINED PRODUCTION PATH DEVIATION: Production --resume presents candidates through ctx.ui.notify but auto-selects most recent thread rather than resolving an explicit operator selection (EV-002). The implementation acknowledges this as a spec deviation due to PI v0.79.2 lacking an interactive input surface.\"\n  ],\n  \"blockingFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"EV-001\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"title\": \"Reload for no-flag and --resume uses cwd-most-recent registry selection instead of reconstructing from the resolved thread id\",\n      \"evidence\": \"AC-1.5 requires reload reconstruction from 'the resolved thread id' (epic.md:137). resolveReloadThread for no-flag/--resume uses listed.value.at(-1) after threads.listThreads({cwd}) (thread-resolution.ts:141-145). The code comment (lines 118-121) acknowledges this as an Epic-1 convenience with 'known concurrent same-cwd limitation' and defers precise lineage to Feature 2+. The production test (thread-resolution.test.ts:335-370) only proves the single-thread-in-cwd case. Story 1 verification (014-verify.json) confirms SV-001 is 'needs-human-ruling' with gates passing but production behavior deviating from AC-1.5.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/thread-resolution.ts\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\",\n        \"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/014-verify.json\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"AC-1.5\",\n        \"TC-1.5\"\n      ],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"human-ruling\",\n      \"blocking\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"EV-002\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"title\": \"Production --resume auto-selects most recent thread instead of resolving an operator selection\",\n      \"evidence\": \"AC-1.7 requires --resume to 'resolve the operator's selection' (epic.md:141). defaultSelectThread (index.ts:191-201) presents candidates via ctx.ui.notify but returns mostRecent.threadId without operator input. The code comment (lines 181-190) acknowledges this as 'a precise spec deviation' because PI v0.79.2 'exposes no interactive input/selection surface'. The production test (thread-resolution.test.ts:255-290) asserts notification plus most-recent behavior as the expected path. Story 1 verification (014-verify.json) confirms SV-002 is 'needs-human-ruling' with gates passing but production behavior deviating from AC-1.7.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/picker.ts\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/test/lifecycle/thread-resolution.test.ts\",\n        \"docs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/artifacts/01-session-lifecycle-and-thread-resolution/014-verify.json\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"AC-1.7\",\n        \"TC-1.7\"\n      ],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"human-ruling\",\n      \"blocking\": true\n    }\n  ],\n  \"nonBlockingFindings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NF-001\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"Documented idempotency edge case for identity-less events\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Story 2 implementation notes SV-001 residual: a truly identity-less event (no entryId AND no source position AND same content) cannot satisfy both stable-on-redelivery AND unique-per-occurrence constraints. Real PI message_end always carries a stable entry id per research, so this edge is unreachable on the production hook path.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"AC-2.6\"\n      ],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"human-ruling\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NF-002\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"PI extension input/selection API unavailable for --resume picker\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Story 1 implementation notes SV-002: PI v0.79.2 exposes no interactive input/selection surface. Production --resume presents candidates via ctx.ui.notify and auto-selects most-recent. Exact operator selection and exact-prior-thread reload are deferred until PI provides the API. This is the root cause of EV-002.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/picker.ts\",\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"AC-1.7\"\n      ],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"fresh-fix-path\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NF-003\",\n      \"severity\": \"observation\",\n      \"title\": \"Derived form reuse optimization deferred for v1\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Story 4 fork implementation always requeues derived forms rather than copying/reusing ready forms. Fork correctness is preserved (AC-3.3 permits reuse 'may'), but provenance-identity safety is not yet implemented. Reuse optimization deferred to Epic 2+.\",\n      \"affectedFiles\": [\n        \"packages/pi-lhc/src/lifecycle/fork.ts\"\n      ],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"AC-3.3\"\n      ],\n      \"recommendedFixScope\": \"fresh-fix-path\",\n      \"blocking\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unresolvedItems\": [\n    \"Human ruling needed: Accept or reject cwd-most-recent registry reattach as satisfying AC-1.5 for Story 1 despite the known concurrent same-cwd limitation documented in thread-resolution.ts:118-121.\",\n    \"Human ruling needed: Accept or reject notify-list plus most-recent default as satisfying AC-1.7 until PI exposes an interactive selection API, as documented in index.ts:181-190.\",\n    \"M0 corpora for Story 3 fixtures — current implementation uses synthetic builders; test coverage widens when M0 delivers recorded PI sessions.\",\n    \"Image/file-reference handling decision (A-7) — interim implementation degrades unsupported parts to runtime_note events with omission text; safe default that can extend intake schema when M0 decides.\",\n    \"PI extension input/selection API — upstream request filed for real --resume picker and exact-thread reload capability.\",\n    \"createSdk→initLh